-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock: Infernal Bargain (was Molten Skin) and Wailing Souls
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- MOLTEN SKIN -> INFERNAL BARGAIN  (talent 1887, ranks 63349/63350/63351)
--   "Channel souls to the nether in exchange for power and protection. For
--    each Soul Shard thrown into the endless void, you do X% more damage and
--    the critical effect chance of your spells is increased by X% for 10
--    seconds. While committing to the pact you are protected by demonic
--    forces, taking X% less damage."
--
--   This converts a passive into an ACTIVE ability, so:
--     - SPELL_ATTR0_PASSIVE (0x40) is cleared: 464 -> 400.
--     - talent_dbc Flags = 1 (addToSpellBook) -- see woa_2026_08_01_02.sql.
--     - SpellFamilyName 8 -> 5 so future Warlock class-mask modifiers see it.
--     - Effect1 becomes SPELL_EFFECT_DUMMY, handled by
--       spell_warl_infernal_bargain (src/WarlockInfernalBargain.cpp).
--
--   Per-rank tuning is carried in the rank spell's own basepoints so that
--   rank scaling stays in the DBC/SQL layer and the C++ has no magic numbers:
--     EffectBasePoints1 = damage % per shard      (2 / 3 / 4)
--     EffectBasePoints2 = spell crit % per shard  (1 / 1 / 2)
--     EffectBasePoints3 = flat damage reduction % (15 / 20 / 25)
--   All three use EffectDieSides = 0, because SpellEffectInfo::CalcValue
--   returns BasePoints unchanged when DieSides is 0 (SpellInfo.cpp:431).
--   Effect2/Effect3 stay 0 -- they are pure data carriers; CalcValue reads
--   the basepoint fields regardless of the effect type.
--
--   Spell 200401 is the resulting 10s buff (DurationIndex 1 = 10000ms,
--   confirmed against Berserking 20554 and Enrage 5229).  Its three amounts
--   are always supplied as custom basepoints by the script.
--   EVERY EffectSpellClassMask is zeroed: SPELL_AURA_MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_DONE
--   with a stray class mask silently applies to nothing.
--
-- NETHER PROTECTION -> WAILING SOULS  (talent 1679, ranks 30299/30301/30302)
--   "Casting Searing Pain transforms a Soul Shard into a Wailing Soul.
--    Wailing Souls reduce damage taken by 15% for 10 seconds. Max 3 stacks."
--
--   Talent ranks become SPELL_AURA_DUMMY proc carriers; the shard-to-soul
--   conversion is spell_warl_wailing_soul (src/WarlockNetherProtection.cpp),
--   because proc-time reagent consumption has no DBC representation.
--
--   Spell 200402 "Wailing Soul" is cloned from 54370 -- Nether Protection's
--   own existing MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_TAKEN buff, the closest possible base.
--   StackAmount = 3 caps the stacks in DBC, so the script never has to.
--   EffectBasePoints1 = -5 gives 5% reduction per stack, 15% at 3 stacks.
--   (For the alternative reading of the TODO -- 15% PER stack, 45% at 3 --
--    change EffectBasePoints1 to -15.)
--   EffectMiscValue1 2 -> 127 so it reduces all schools, not just Holy.
-- ===========================================================================


